[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 703,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 466,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105459,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 480,
        "headingId": 466,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Fibrous hamartoma of infancy (FHI) is a soft tissue neoplasm of infants and young children, showing a characteristic organoid, triphasic morphology with bundles of bland fibroblastic/myofibroblastic cells, nodules of primitive mesenchyme, and mature adipose tissue.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:27:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 704,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 467,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105460,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 480,
        "headingId": 467,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8992/0 Fibrous hamartoma of infancy</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:27:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 705,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 468,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105461,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 480,
        "headingId": 468,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>LC2Y Other specified hamartomata derived from dermal connective tissue</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:27:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 706,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 469,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105462,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 480,
        "headingId": 469,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> subdermal fibromatous tumour of infancy.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:27:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 707,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 470,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105463,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 480,
        "headingId": 470,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:27:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 708,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 471,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105464,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 480,
        "headingId": 471,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>FHI commonly involves the axillae, trunk, upper extremities, and genital region. Other locations include the scalp, foot, hand, orbit, and buttock {28059097; 24525510}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:27:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 709,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 472,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105465,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 480,
        "headingId": 472,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients with FHI present with a painless solitary subcutaneous mass, sometimes with overlying skin discolouration, oedema, hypertrichosis, and tethering {28059097}. Large lesions and multiple tumours in the same patient can be encountered. FHI has been reported in patients with tuberous sclerosis and William syndrome {28059097; 19319513; 17326745}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:27:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 710,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 473,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105466,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 480,
        "headingId": 473,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>FHI is rare, generally diagnosed by 2&nbsp;years of age, with a male predominance. It is congenital in 15&ndash;25% of cases {24525510}. Occurrence in older children is possible {28059097}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:27:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 711,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 474,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105467,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 480,
        "headingId": 474,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:27:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 712,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 475,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105468,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 480,
        "headingId": 475,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Recurrent <em>EGFR</em> exon&nbsp;20 insertion/duplication mutations have been demonstrated in these lesions {27631514}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:27:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 719,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 482,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105469,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 480,
        "headingId": 482,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>FHI is poorly circumscribed and ranges in size from 4&nbsp;to 170&nbsp;mm (mean: 30&nbsp;mm), with a variable amount of adipose tissue and grey-tan fibrous tissue {28059097}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:27:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 713,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 476,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105470,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 480,
        "headingId": 476,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>FHI has a characteristic triphasic organoid pattern with fascicles of bland fibroblastic/myofibroblastic cells admixed with mature adipose tissue and myxoid nodules containing primitive mesenchymal cells with rounded to stellate nuclei. One&nbsp;quarter of cases can show areas resembling giant cell fibroblastoma and composed of hyalinized zones containing collagen with cracking artefact forming slit-like spaces lined by flattened tumour cells. Mitotic figures are infrequent, and necrosis is typically absent. Interspersed inflammatory cells can be seen. Sarcomatous morphology has been reported in two tumours {28059097}.</p>\r\n<p>By immunohistochemistry, FHI shows variable expression of SMA in the fibroblastic areas and in primitive mesenchyme. S100 is expressed in the adipocytic component. Primitive mesenchyme and areas with giant cell fibroblastoma&ndash;like morphology are CD34-positive. Minimal to moderate EGFR protein expression has been reported, mostly in the primitive mesenchyme {27631514}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:27:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 714,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 477,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105471,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 480,
        "headingId": 477,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>FNAB-produced smears show bland fibroblasts in a collagenous matrix and mature fat without nuclear atypia or mitoses {18499982}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:27:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 715,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 478,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105472,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 480,
        "headingId": 478,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>EGFR</em> exon&nbsp;20 insertion/duplication mutations have been identified cases of FHI by targeted next-generation sequencing and Sanger sequencing {27631514}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:27:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 718,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 481,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105473,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 480,
        "headingId": 481,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> characteristic triphasic morphology with bundles of bland fibroblastic/myofibroblastic cells, nodules of primitive mesenchyme, and mature adipose tissue.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> EGFR expression.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:27:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 716,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 479,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105474,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 480,
        "headingId": 479,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:27:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 717,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 480,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 105475,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 480,
        "headingId": 480,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most patients are cured with simple excision, although roughly 15% of cases have been reported to locally recur if incompletely excised.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-15T11:27:28"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]